Hi Hua,

You can use the methylRawList() or methylRawListDB() constructor to put the objects in the same list, as described in section "6.0.20 How can I merge multiple separate methylRaw objects into a methylRawList?" of the FAQ section <https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/methylKit/inst/doc/methylKit.html#6_Frequently_Asked_Questions>.

However, these constructors will only accept objects of the same type, so you have to convert them to either normal or *DB objects. Please check here <https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/methylKit/inst/doc/methylKit.html#5_methylKit_convenience_functions> for instructions on how to convert the types.

Best,
Alex
